In article <25gq9kINNg1h@borg.cs.unc.edu>, leech@cs.unc.edu (Jon Leech) writes:
>     I seem to keep polymorphing into some incredibly wimpy monster - and
> destroying my (fairly nice, by then) armor - after being on the bottom level
> of the Mines for a while. Is this something that will always happen? Why? Is
> there any way to avoid it?

Yes, you can avoid it. Don't put your ring of polymorph on. Ring of
searching also helps detecting the traps early...

Now, if I'm already at the topic of polymorph: there's a very annoying
asymmetry between monsters and players: if a player steps on a polymorph
trap, the trap disappears. If a monster does - it stays. I understand why
the traps disappear for players (to avoid abuse), but a polymorph trap in
the mines usually means that I'll have to fight two dragons, two trolls and
an ice devil (that's from my recent game). These ... gnomes are clever
enough to step on it repeatedly until they become really powerful. Even if
I manage to escape - the mines are effectively locked for me until much
later, when I'm more powerful. Plus, whenever I find a polymorph trap I
have to step on it (accepting any risks, including death of system shock) -
just to avoid a nasty surprise later... Oh Great Dev. Team who live upon
The Net, could we worms please have this better balanced? Our prayers
concerning 'sleep asymmetry' have been heard - could this one be heard as
well?

